From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: soc: sunxi: cpu_comm: a parked core answers -ENODEV as promised, not -EBUSY

The park's message and cpu_comm.h say kernel RPCs fail with -ENODEV while
the core is parked, but the park takes the suspend count as well, and
cpu_comm_call() tested that count first: a parked core answered -EBUSY,
the code of "being replaced, try again". A caller that tells the two apart
(hdmirx's SetSource after a wake) tried again in vain and the log named
a code the message did not. The parked test now comes first. Review of
09.10.2026, CC-3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_api.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_api.c
@@ -169,6 +169,15 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	if (!ShMemAddrBase || !pcpu_comm_dev)
 		return -ENODEV;
+	/*
+	 * Parked for the standby: -ENODEV, as the park's message and the
+	 * header promise. Before the count, which the park takes as well -
+	 * through it alone a parked core read as "being replaced" (-EBUSY),
+	 * and a caller that tells the two apart tried again in vain (review
+	 * 09.10., CC-3).
+	 */
+	if (READ_ONCE(cpu_comm_parked_since))
+		return -ENODEV;
 	/* The core is being replaced (cpu_comm_firmware_stop). */
 	if (cpu_comm_suspend_flag > 0)
 		return -EBUSY;
